## 5️⃣ Practical Tips for the Sydney → Melbourne Road Trip

| Tip | Reason / How‑to |
|-----|-----------------|
| **Route** | The fastest route is the **Hume Highway (M31)** – ~ 878 km, ~ 9 h 30 m driving time. |
| **Fuel stops** | Even with the hybrid’s excellent economy, a quick top‑up near **Goulburn** (mid‑way) keeps you away from premium airport fuel prices. |
| **Rest breaks** | Stop at **Canberra** (optional detour to Parliament House) – adds ~ 30 min but makes the drive more enjoyable. |
| **Tolls** | The Hume Highway is toll‑free. If you choose the scenic **Princes Highway (A1)**, expect tolls of AU$5‑10. |
| **Parking at MEL** | Avis offers short‑term parking (AU$25 / day) for drop‑off vehicles; you can also drop the car off curbside at the terminal (no extra charge). |
| **Weather** | Late‑November is late spring – daytime temps 22‑28 °C, occasional showers. Keep windshield wipers handy. |
| **Documentation** | Bring a valid driver’s licence, credit card for the security deposit, and the reservation confirmation number. |

---

## 6️⃣ Quick FAQ

| Question | Answer |
|----------|--------|
| **Can I change the drop‑off location?** | Yes, up to 24 h before the scheduled drop‑off. A location‑change fee (≈ AU$30) may apply. |
| **What documents are required at pick‑up?** | Valid driver’s licence, credit card for the security deposit, and the reservation confirmation number. |
| **Is there a mileage limit?** | No – the rental includes unlimited kilometres. |
| **What if I return the car late?** | Late‑return fee is AU$25 per hour (or part thereof) after a 30‑minute grace period. |
| **Can I pick‑up the car earlier on the same day?** | Early pick‑up is possible if the vehicle is available; a pro‑rated charge of AU$15 / hour applies. |
| **Do I need to purchase insurance?** | The optional CDW/TP/PAI package (AU$20 /day) removes most out‑of‑pocket risk. If you have a credit‑card travel insurance that covers rental cars, you may decline it, but be aware of any deductible that may apply. |

